[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged every date report into one ticket and marked it known. The
reports do not share one cause. Read one at a time, they fall into three problems, each with its
own ticket in the public repo
[woocache/ticket-4471-causes](https://github.com/woocache/ticket-4471-causes).

<Callout>
Not one issue. A fix for the parser alone leaves two problems open.
</Callout>

## What the reports say

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## The three problems

1. **The parser reads dates month first.** Tenants that write the day first get flipped dates. This
   is the cause `parser`, and the largest group. Ticket:
   [issue 1](https://github.com/woocache/ticket-4471-causes/issues/1).
2. **The booking-v3 form prints a month-first hint.** People at day-first tenants type what the
   hint tells them, and the form reads it their way. This is the cause `hint`, and only form
   reports show it. Ticket: [issue 2](https://github.com/woocache/ticket-4471-causes/issues/2).
3. **Some invites move by exactly one day.** The desk read a few reports this way (see the note
   under the table). The date is not month-flipped, so the parser fix does not explain them. The
   cause is not yet investigated. Ticket:
   [issue 3](https://github.com/woocache/ticket-4471-causes/issues/3).

## Why #4471 hid this

Intake tags a report from the reporter's browser, which is a guess. The cause depends on the
tenant's locale and booking form, so the tag and the cause disagree (see the "tagged as" column).
Merging by subject ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) never looks at either.

## Lessons

- Count by cause, not by subject. Merging early hides a second bug behind the first.
- A ticket marked known should still say how many causes its reports hold.

